  "description": "PAZTIT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H140 Gd4 N9 Na5 O14 Si6,C4 H8 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.661-3.729 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.34-112.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(μ4-O)(NHPh)3(OSiMe2NPh)6Na5(thf)7]·THF / C99H137Gd4N9Na5O14Si6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
